      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠ Common Traps & Exam Pitfalls",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Variance formula trap:</strong> Remember \\(\\text{Var}(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2\\). Do not forget to square \\(E(X)\\), and do not compute \\(E(X^2) - E(X)\\).<br><br><strong>Linear coding of variance:</strong> \\(\\text{Var}(aX + b) = a^2 \\text{Var}(X)\\). Notice that the constant \\(b\\) is eliminated completely, and a negative multiplier \\(a\\) becomes positive due to squaring (e.g. \\(\\text{Var}(5 - 2X) = (-2)^2 \\text{Var}(X) = 4\\text{Var}(X)\\)).<br><br><strong>Sum of probabilities:</strong> The total probability MUST sum to 1: \\(\\sum P(X = x) = 1\\). Always verify this condition first when solving for unknown parameters \\(p\\) or \\(k\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding E(X) and Var(X)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A biased die shows: \\(P(1)=0.1,P(2)=0.2,P(3)=0.3,P(4)=0.3,P(5)=0.1\\). Find \\(E(X)\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(X)\\).</p>\\[E(X)=0.1(1)+0.2(2)+0.3(3)+0.3(4)+0.1(5)=0.1+0.4+0.9+1.2+0.5=3.1.\\]\\[E(X^2)=0.1(1)+0.2(4)+0.3(9)+0.3(16)+0.1(25)=0.1+0.8+2.7+4.8+2.5=10.9.\\]\\[\\text{Var}(X)=10.9-3.1^2=10.9-9.61=1.29.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Unknown probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\) takes values 0, 1, 2 with \\(P(X=0)=k\\), \\(P(X=1)=2k\\), \\(P(X=2)=3k\\). Find \\(k\\) and \\(E(X)\\).</p>\\[k+2k+3k=1\\Rightarrow k=\\tfrac{1}{6}.\\quad E(X)=0\\cdot\\tfrac{1}{6}+1\\cdot\\tfrac{2}{6}+2\\cdot\\tfrac{3}{6}=\\tfrac{8}{6}=\\tfrac{4}{3}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example C — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 13x + 36 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 4)(x - 9) = 0 \\implies x = 4 \\text{ or } x = 9 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 4 + 9 = \\mathbf{13} \\) and product \\( = (4)(9) = \\mathbf{36} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example D — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 10x + 25 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 5)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = 5 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 5 + 5 = \\mathbf{10} \\) and product \\( = (5)(5) = \\mathbf{25} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "\\(E(X)=3\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(X)=2\\). Find \\(E(3X-1)\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(3X-1)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(E(3X-1)=3(3)-1=8\\). \\(\\text{Var}(3X-1)=9\\times2=18\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A discrete random variable \\(Y\\) has \\(E(Y) = 5\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(Y) = 4\\). Calculate \\(E(Y^2)\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(10 - 3Y)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Using \\(\\text{Var}(Y) = E(Y^2) - [E(Y)]^2\\), we get \\(E(Y^2) = \\text{Var}(Y) + [E(Y)]^2 = 4 + 5^2 = 4 + 25 = 29\\). For the linear transformation: \\(\\text{Var}(10 - 3Y) = (-3)^2 \\text{Var}(Y) = 9 \\times 4 = 36\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
