      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "[Discrete Random Variables · Practice 3] If the governing relation for this system is \\( g(t) = 5t + 5 \\), evaluate \\( g(8) \\) and find the inverse input \\( t \\) when \\( g(t) = 50 \\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Substitute \\( t = 8 \\): \\( g(8) = 5(8) + 5 = \\mathbf{45} \\). Setting \\( 5t + 5 = 50 \\) gives \\( 5t = 45 \\implies t = \\mathbf{9} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "[Discrete Random Variables · Practice 4] If the governing relation for this system is \\( g(t) = 6t + 6 \\), evaluate \\( g(10) \\) and find the inverse input \\( t \\) when \\( g(t) = 72 \\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Substitute \\( t = 10 \\): \\( g(10) = 6(10) + 6 = \\mathbf{66} \\). Setting \\( 6t + 6 = 72 \\) gives \\( 6t = 66 \\implies t = \\mathbf{11} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
